# 3. LOGIN AND AUTHENTICATION SYSTEM

Use Firebase Authentication with Google Sign-In.

The login page must contain only TWO main login buttons:

1. Student Login
2. Faculty Login

There must be NO separate Admin Login button.

## Login behaviour

When a user clicks Student Login:
- Open Google's account selection screen.
- Allow the user to select their Google account.
- Authenticate using Firebase.
- Verify whether the account is registered as a student.
- Redirect to Student Dashboard.

When a user clicks Faculty Login:
- Open Google's account selection screen.
- Authenticate using Firebase.
- Verify whether the account is registered as faculty.
- Redirect to Faculty Dashboard.

## Special admin login behaviour

Admin login must happen automatically.

For example:

If the authorized admin selects their Google account, the application must identify the admin role and redirect directly to Admin Dashboard.

There must be no visible Admin Login button.

This must work regardless of which login button was initially clicked.

The role must be verified using trusted Firebase records or custom claims.

## Security

- Students cannot assign themselves faculty or admin roles.
- Faculty cannot assign themselves admin roles.
- Unregistered accounts must not receive dashboard access.
- Admin accounts must be authorized through a trusted setup process.
- Include logout.
- Include account switching.
- Include proper authentication error handling.

Use Google's account chooser so users can select between multiple Google accounts.

